// The player's XP multiplier: 1, 5 or 10, or 0 for "never chosen" (which the engine reads as 1).
//
// scope=perm because it is the account's for good - it is chosen once on Tutorial Island and
// ~xprate_choose refuses to ask again once the tutorial is complete, so a finished account can
// never move itself onto a faster rate.
//
// NOT transmitted. The first draft was, so the chooser's boxes could highlight the chosen mode
// client-side - but ~xprate_choose returns early once a rate is set, so the window is only ever
// open while the rate is unset and there is never anything to highlight. The client has no other
// use for the number; the engine reads it server-side in Player.addXp.
[xp_rate]
scope=perm

// Which skills refuse experience, one bit each, at the skill's own index in the
// engine's stat order - see ^xplock_* in gamemode.constant. Read by Player.addXp,
// which returns before the experience is added.
//
// scope=perm because a lock is the account's until the player lifts it. NOT
// transmitted: the client has no use for it, and the stats tab's LOCKED markers are
// pushed as text by ~xplock_restore at login rather than driven from a varp.
[xp_locked]
scope=perm
